## Objective

The objective of this feature is to allow recruiters to manage
their previously created job postings.

The recruiter should be able to:

- Edit job details
- Delete a job posting
- Close a job posting
- View the current job status
- Manage postings only after authentication

---

## Main Workflow

Recruiter Login
        |
        v
Recruiter Dashboard
        |
        v
Manage Job Postings
        |
        +------> Edit Job
        |
        +------> Close Job
        |
        +------> Delete Job
        |
        v
Database

---

## Edit Job

The recruiter can modify information such as:

- Job title
- Job description
- Location
- Eligibility
- Salary
- Application deadline

Before updating the database, the application validates
required fields.

---

## Delete Job

The recruiter can permanently remove a job posting.

A confirmation message is shown before deletion to reduce
accidental deletion.

---

## Close Job

Closing a job is different from deleting it.

A closed job remains stored in the system but is no longer
available for new applications.

The job status should become:

CLOSED

---

## Authentication

Only an authenticated recruiter should be allowed to access
the job management page.

The servlet checks:

session.getAttribute("userId")

If the user is not logged in, the application redirects
the user to the login page.

